Release/self-update is validated entirely through the project's own automated
tests (internal/update/), never against a real installed system, per the
project's own safe-by-design update path (checksum + mandatory-once-configured
ed25519 signature verification, a real execution of the new binary's
--version before anything is replaced, old binaries kept, and separate
config knobs for "check" vs. "apply").

On Windows:
$ CGO_ENABLED=0 go test ./internal/update/... -v
25 tests, 20 PASS, 5 SKIP (skipped ones actually execute installed binaries
and real file-mode/exec-bit semantics - guarded to Linux).

On Linux (WSL2 netrewind-lab, run against the same source tree via the
/mnt/c/netrewind-src junction):
$ CGO_ENABLED=0 go test ./internal/update/... -v
